GIVEN `the court or Review Board is making a disposition under subsection 672.45(2), section 672.47, subsection 672.64(3) or section 672.83 or 672.84` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a verdict of not criminally responsible on account of mental disorder has been rendered in respect of the accused` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the accused is a significant threat to the safety of the public, in the opinion of the court or Review Board, by s 672.5401` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A LIST OF `s 672.54 disposition`
`s 672.54 the dispositions that are open` MEANS
    IF NOT `the court or Review Board is making a disposition under subsection 672.45(2), section 672.47, subsection 672.64(3) or section 672.83 or 672.84`
    THEN EMPTY
    ELSE IF `s 672.54(a) the court or Review Board may direct that the accused be discharged absolutely` `a verdict of not criminally responsible on account of mental disorder has been rendered in respect of the accused` `the accused is a significant threat to the safety of the public, in the opinion of the court or Review Board, by s 672.5401` EQUALS JUST TRUE
         THEN LIST `s 672.54(a) a discharge absolutely`, `s 672.54(b) a discharge subject to conditions`, `s 672.54(c) detention in custody in a hospital, subject to conditions`
         ELSE LIST `s 672.54(b) a discharge subject to conditions`, `s 672.54(c) detention in custody in a hospital, subject to conditions`

-- 672.541: if a verdict of NCR has been rendered, the court or Review Board shall (a) at a hearing under 672.45, 672.47, 672.64, 672.81 or 672.82 or subsection 672.84(5), take into consideration any statement filed by a victim under 672.5(14) in determining the appropriate disposition or conditions under 672.54, to the extent that it is relevant;
-- (b) at a hearing under 672.64 or subsection 672.84(3), take it into consideration in deciding whether to find that the accused is a high-risk accused, or to revoke such a finding; and (c) at a hearing under 672.81 or 672.82 in respect of a high-risk accused, take it into consideration in determining whether to refer to the court for review the finding that the accused is a high-risk accused.
-- fork: F-DUTY-GATE
-- src:13743 | 672.541 If a verdict of not criminally responsible on account of mental disorder has been rendered in respect of an accused, the court or Review Board shall
-- src:13744 | (a) at a hearing held under section 672.45, 672.47, 672.64, 672.81 or 672.82 or subsection 672.84(5), take into consideration any statement filed by a victim in accordance with subsection 672.5(14) in determining the appropriate disposition or conditions under section 672.54, to the extent that the statement is relevant to its consideration of the criteria set out in section 672.54;
-- src:13745 | (b) at a hearing held under section 672.64 or subsection 672.84(3), take into consideration any statement filed by a victim in accordance with subsection 672.5(14), to the extent that the statement is relevant to its consideration of the criteria set out in subsection 672.64(1) or 672.84(3), as the case may be, in deciding whether to find that the accused is a high-risk accused, or to revoke such a finding; and
-- src:13746 | (c) at a hearing held under section 672.81 or 672.82 in respect of a high-risk accused, take into consideration any statement filed by a victim in accordance with subsection 672.5(14) in determining whether to refer to the court for review the finding that the accused is a high-risk accused, to the extent that the statement is relevant to its consideration of the criteria set out in subsection 672.84(1).
@ref s 672.541; s 672.541(a); s 672.541(b); s 672.541(c) (src:13743-13746)
GIVEN `a verdict of not criminally responsible on account of mental disorder has been rendered` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a statement has been filed by a victim in accordance with subsection 672.5(14)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a hearing under section 672.45, 672.47, 672.64, 672.81 or 672.82 or subsection 672.84(5), to determine the appropriate disposition or conditions under section 672.54` IS A BOOLEAN   -- (a)
      `it is a hearing under section 672.64 or subsection 672.84(3), to decide whether to find that the accused is a high-risk accused or to revoke such a finding` IS A BOOLEAN   -- (b)
      `it is a hearing under section 672.81 or 672.82 in respect of a high-risk accused, to determine whether to refer the finding to the court for review` IS A BOOLEAN   -- (c)
      `the statement is relevant to the criteria in section 672.54, subsection 672.64(1) or 672.84(3), or subsection 672.84(1), as the case may be` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 672.541 the court or Review Board must take the victim’s statement into consideration` MEANS
    IF `a verdict of not criminally responsible on account of mental disorder has been rendered` AND `a statement has been filed by a victim in accordance with subsection 672.5(14)` AND (`it is a hearing under section 672.45, 672.47, 672.64, 672.81 or 672.82 or subsection 672.84(5), to determine the appropriate disposition or conditions under section 672.54` OR `it is a hearing under section 672.64 or subsection 672.84(3), to decide whether to find that the accused is a high-risk accused or to revoke such a finding` OR `it is a hearing under section 672.81 or 672.82 in respect of a high-risk accused, to determine whether to refer the finding to the court for review`) AND `the statement is relevant to the criteria in section 672.54, subsection 672.64(1) or 672.84(3), or subsection 672.84(1), as the case may be`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "to the extent that the statement is relevant to its consideration of the criteria"

-- 672.542: when a court or Review Board holds a hearing referred to in section 672.5, it shall consider whether it is desirable, in the interests of the safety and security of any person, particularly a victim of or witness to the offence or a justice system participant, to include as a condition of the disposition
-- that the accused (a) abstain from communicating, directly or indirectly, with any victim, witness or other person identified in the disposition, or refrain from going to any place specified in the disposition; or (b) comply with any other condition specified in the disposition that the court or Review Board considers necessary to ensure the safety and security of those persons.
-- fork: F-DUTY-GATE
