§ `Sections 672.55 to 672.57 -- Treatment, delegation, committal`

-- 672.55(1): no disposition made under section 672.54 shall direct that any psychiatric or other treatment of the accused be carried out or that the accused submit to such treatment, except that the disposition may include a condition regarding psychiatric or other treatment
-- where the accused has consented to the condition and the court or Review Board considers the condition to be reasonable and necessary in the interests of the accused. Named as the bar: JUST FALSE = the text's own exception is met.
-- fork: F-BAR-IF
-- src:13752 | 672.55 (1) No disposition made under section 672.54 shall direct that any psychiatric or other treatment of the accused be carried out or that the accused submit to such treatment except that the disposition may include a condition regarding psychiatric or other treatment where the accused has consented to the condition and the court or Review Board considers the condition to be reasonable and necessary in the interests of the accused.
@ref s 672.55(1) (src:13752)
GIVEN `the disposition directs that any psychiatric or other treatment of the accused be carried out or that the accused submit to such treatment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the accused has consented to the condition` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court or Review Board considers the condition to be reasonable and necessary in the interests of the accused` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 672.55(1) the section bars the disposition from directing treatment` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the disposition directs that any psychiatric or other treatment of the accused be carried out or that the accused submit to such treatment` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "No disposition made under section 672.54 shall direct that any psychiatric or other treatment of the accused be carried out"
        IF `the accused has consented to the condition` AND `the court or Review Board considers the condition to be reasonable and necessary in the interests of the accused` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "except that the disposition may include a condition regarding psychiatric or other treatment where the accused has consented to the condition"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

