-- 672.56(1): a Review Board that makes a disposition in respect of an accused under paragraph 672.54(b) or (c) may delegate to the person in charge of the hospital authority to direct that the restrictions on the liberty of the accused be increased or decreased within any limits and subject to any conditions
-- set out in that disposition, and any direction so made is deemed for the purposes of this Act to be a disposition made by the Review Board.
