-- 672.56(2): a person who increases the restrictions on the liberty of the accused significantly pursuant to authority delegated by a Review Board shall (a) make a record of the increased restrictions on the file of the accused; and
-- (b) give notice of the increase as soon as is practicable to the accused and, if the increased restrictions remain in force for a period exceeding seven days, to the Review Board.
