§ `Sections 672.58 to 672.62 -- Treatment disposition for an accused found unfit`

-- 672.58: where a verdict of unfit to stand trial is rendered and the court has not made a disposition under section 672.54 in respect of an accused, the court may, on application by the prosecutor, by order, direct that treatment of the accused be carried out for a specified period not exceeding sixty days,
-- subject to such conditions as the court considers appropriate and, where the accused is not detained in custody, direct that the accused submit to that treatment by the person or at the hospital specified.
-- fork: F-GRANT-WHERE
-- src:13765 | 672.58 Where a verdict of unfit to stand trial is rendered and the court has not made a disposition under section 672.54 in respect of an accused, the court may, on application by the prosecutor, by order, direct that treatment of the accused be carried out for a specified period not exceeding sixty days, subject to such conditions as the court considers appropriate and, where the accused is not detained in custody, direct that the accused submit to that treatment by the person or at the hospital specified.
@ref s 672.58 (src:13765)
GIVEN `a verdict of unfit to stand trial is rendered` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court has not made a disposition under section 672.54 in respect of the accused` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the prosecutor applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the days of the specified period` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 672.58 the court may direct that treatment of the accused be carried out` MEANS
    IF `a verdict of unfit to stand trial is rendered` AND `the court has not made a disposition under section 672.54 in respect of the accused` AND `the prosecutor applies` AND `the days of the specified period` AT MOST 60
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a verdict of unfit to stand trial is rendered and the court has not made a disposition under section 672.54 in respect of an accused, the court may, on application by the prosecutor"

-- 672.59(1): no disposition may be made under section 672.58 unless the court is satisfied, on the basis of the testimony of a medical practitioner, that a specific treatment should be administered to the accused for the purpose of making the accused fit to stand trial. Named as the bar.
-- src:13767 | 672.59 (1) No disposition may be made under section 672.58 unless the court is satisfied, on the basis of the testimony of a medical practitioner, that a specific treatment should be administered to the accused for the purpose of making the accused fit to stand trial.
@ref s 672.59(1) (src:13767)
GIVEN `the court is satisfied, on the basis of the testimony of a medical practitioner, that a specific treatment should be administered to the accused for the purpose of making the accused fit to stand trial` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 672.59(1) the court is barred from making a disposition under section 672.58` MEANS
    IF `the court is satisfied, on the basis of the testimony of a medical practitioner, that a specific treatment should be administered to the accused for the purpose of making the accused fit to stand trial`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "No disposition may be made under section 672.58 unless the court is satisfied, on the basis of the testimony of a medical practitioner"
    ELSE JUST TRUE

-- 672.59(2): the testimony required for the purposes of (1) shall include a statement that the medical practitioner has made an assessment of the accused and is of the opinion, based on the grounds specified, that (a) the accused, at the time of the assessment, was unfit to stand trial;
-- (b) the psychiatric treatment and any other related medical treatment specified will likely make the accused fit within a period not exceeding sixty days and that without that treatment the accused is likely to remain unfit; (c) the risk of harm to the accused from the treatment is not disproportionate to the benefit anticipated;
-- and (d) the treatment specified is the least restrictive and least intrusive treatment that could, in the circumstances, be specified, considering the opinions in (b) and (c).
-- fork: F-MUST-BARE
-- src:13769 | (2) The testimony required by the court for the purposes of subsection (1) shall include a statement that the medical practitioner has made an assessment of the accused and is of the opinion, based on the grounds specified, that
-- src:13770 | (a) the accused, at the time of the assessment, was unfit to stand trial;
-- src:13771 | (b) the psychiatric treatment and any other related medical treatment specified by the medical practitioner will likely make the accused fit to stand trial within a period not exceeding sixty days and that without that treatment the accused is likely to remain unfit to stand trial;
-- src:13772 | (c) the risk of harm to the accused from the psychiatric and other related medical treatment specified is not disproportionate to the benefit anticipated to be derived from it; and
-- src:13773 | (d) the psychiatric and other related medical treatment specified is the least restrictive and least intrusive treatment that could, in the circumstances, be specified for the purpose referred to in subsection (1), considering the opinions referred to in paragraphs (b) and (c).
@ref s 672.59(2); s 672.59(2)(a); s 672.59(2)(b); s 672.59(2)(c); s 672.59(2)(d) (src:13769-13773)
GIVEN `the testimony includes a statement that the medical practitioner has made an assessment of the accused` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the statement gives the opinion, based on the grounds specified, that the accused, at the time of the assessment, was unfit to stand trial` IS A BOOLEAN   -- (a)
      `the statement gives the opinion that the treatment specified will likely make the accused fit to stand trial within a period not exceeding sixty days and that without that treatment the accused is likely to remain unfit to stand trial` IS A BOOLEAN   -- (b)
      `the statement gives the opinion that the risk of harm to the accused from the treatment specified is not disproportionate to the benefit anticipated to be derived from it` IS A BOOLEAN   -- (c)
      `the statement gives the opinion that the treatment specified is the least restrictive and least intrusive treatment that could, in the circumstances, be specified` IS A BOOLEAN   -- (d)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 672.59(2) the testimony includes the statement the subsection requires` MEANS
    IF `the testimony includes a statement that the medical practitioner has made an assessment of the accused` AND `the statement gives the opinion, based on the grounds specified, that the accused, at the time of the assessment, was unfit to stand trial` AND `the statement gives the opinion that the treatment specified will likely make the accused fit to stand trial within a period not exceeding sixty days and that without that treatment the accused is likely to remain unfit to stand trial` AND `the statement gives the opinion that the risk of harm to the accused from the treatment specified is not disproportionate to the benefit anticipated to be derived from it` AND `the statement gives the opinion that the treatment specified is the least restrictive and least intrusive treatment that could, in the circumstances, be specified`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall include a statement that the medical practitioner has made an assessment of the accused"

-- 672.6(1): the court shall not make a disposition under section 672.58 unless the prosecutor notifies the accused, in writing and as soon as practicable, of the application. Named as the bar.
-- src:13775 | 672.6 (1) The court shall not make a disposition under section 672.58 unless the prosecutor notifies the accused, in writing and as soon as practicable, of the application.
@ref s 672.6(1) (src:13775)
GIVEN `the prosecutor notifies the accused, in writing and as soon as practicable, of the application` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 672.6(1) the court is barred from making a disposition under section 672.58` MEANS
    IF `the prosecutor notifies the accused, in writing and as soon as practicable, of the application`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless the prosecutor notifies the accused, in writing and as soon as practicable, of the application"
    ELSE JUST TRUE

-- 672.6(2): on receiving the notice referred to in subsection (1), the accused may challenge the application and adduce evidence for that purpose.
-- fork: F-GRANT-WHERE
-- src:13777 | (2) On receiving the notice referred to in subsection (1), the accused may challenge the application and adduce evidence for that purpose.
@ref s 672.6(2) (src:13777)
GIVEN `the accused receives the notice referred to in subsection 672.6(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 672.6(2) the accused may challenge the application and adduce evidence for that purpose` MEANS
    IF `the accused receives the notice referred to in subsection 672.6(1)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "On receiving the notice referred to in subsection (1)"

-- 672.61(2): electro-convulsive therapy means a procedure for the treatment of certain mental disorders that induces, by electrical stimulation of the brain, a series of generalized convulsions;
-- psychosurgery means any procedure that by direct or indirect access to the brain removes, destroys or interrupts the continuity of histologically normal brain tissue, or inserts indwelling electrodes for pulsed electrical stimulation for the purpose of altering behaviour or treating psychiatric illness,
-- but does not include neurological procedures used to diagnose or treat intractable physical pain, organic brain conditions, or epilepsy, where any of those conditions is clearly demonstrable.
-- src:13782 | electro-convulsive therapy means a procedure for the treatment of certain mental disorders that induces, by electrical stimulation of the brain, a series of generalized convulsions; (sismothérapie)
@ref s 672.61(2); s 672.61(2)"electro-convulsive therapy" (src:13782)
GIVEN `it is a procedure for the treatment of certain mental disorders` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it induces, by electrical stimulation of the brain, a series of generalized convulsions` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 672.61(2) electro-convulsive therapy` MEANS
    IF `it is a procedure for the treatment of certain mental disorders` AND `it induces, by electrical stimulation of the brain, a series of generalized convulsions`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "electro-convulsive therapy means a procedure for the treatment of certain mental disorders that induces, by electrical stimulation of the brain, a series of generalized convulsions"

-- src:13783 | psychosurgery means any procedure that by direct or indirect access to the brain removes, destroys or interrupts the continuity of histologically normal brain tissue, or inserts indwelling electrodes for pulsed electrical stimulation for the purpose of altering behaviour or treating psychiatric illness, but does not include neurological procedures used to diagnose or treat intractable physical pain, organic brain conditions, or epilepsy, where any of those conditions is clearly demonstrable. (psychochirurgie)
@ref s 672.61(2)"psychosurgery" (src:13783)
GIVEN `it is a procedure that by direct or indirect access to the brain removes, destroys or interrupts the continuity of histologically normal brain tissue, or inserts indwelling electrodes for pulsed electrical stimulation for the purpose of altering behaviour or treating psychiatric illness` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a neurological procedure used to diagnose or treat intractable physical pain, organic brain conditions, or epilepsy, where any of those conditions is clearly demonstrable` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 672.61(2) psychosurgery` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `it is a neurological procedure used to diagnose or treat intractable physical pain, organic brain conditions, or epilepsy, where any of those conditions is clearly demonstrable` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "but does not include neurological procedures used to diagnose or treat intractable physical pain, organic brain conditions, or epilepsy"
        IF `it is a procedure that by direct or indirect access to the brain removes, destroys or interrupts the continuity of histologically normal brain tissue, or inserts indwelling electrodes for pulsed electrical stimulation for the purpose of altering behaviour or treating psychiatric illness` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "psychosurgery means any procedure that by direct or indirect access to the brain removes, destroys or interrupts the continuity of histologically normal brain tissue"

-- 672.61(1): the court shall not direct, and no disposition made under section 672.58 shall include, the performance of psychosurgery or electro-convulsive therapy or any other prohibited treatment that is prescribed. Named as the bar.
-- src:13779 | 672.61 (1) The court shall not direct, and no disposition made under section 672.58 shall include, the performance of psychosurgery or electro-convulsive therapy or any other prohibited treatment that is prescribed.
@ref s 672.61(1) (src:13779)
GIVEN `it is psychosurgery, by s 672.61(2)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `it is electro-convulsive therapy, by s 672.61(2)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `it is another prohibited treatment that is prescribed, by s 672.1(1) prescribed` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 672.61(1) the section bars psychosurgery, electro-convulsive therapy or another prescribed prohibited treatment` MEANS
    IF `it is psychosurgery, by s 672.61(2)` EQUALS JUST TRUE OR `it is electro-convulsive therapy, by s 672.61(2)` EQUALS JUST TRUE OR `it is another prohibited treatment that is prescribed, by s 672.1(1) prescribed` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the performance of psychosurgery or electro-convulsive therapy or any other prohibited treatment that is prescribed"

-- 672.62(1): no court shall make a disposition under section 672.58 without the consent of (a) the person in charge of the hospital where the accused is to be treated; or (b) the person to whom responsibility for the treatment of the accused is assigned by the court. Named as the bar.
-- fork: F-WITHOUT-CONSENT
-- src:13785 | 672.62 (1) No court shall make a disposition under section 672.58 without the consent of
-- src:13786 | (a) the person in charge of the hospital where the accused is to be treated; or
-- src:13787 | (b) the person to whom responsibility for the treatment of the accused is assigned by the court.
@ref s 672.62(1); s 672.62(1)(a); s 672.62(1)(b) (src:13785-13787)
GIVEN `the person in charge of the hospital where the accused is to be treated consents` IS A BOOLEAN   -- (a)
      `the person to whom responsibility for the treatment of the accused is assigned by the court consents` IS A BOOLEAN   -- (b)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 672.62(1) the court is barred from making a disposition under section 672.58 without consent` MEANS
    IF `the person in charge of the hospital where the accused is to be treated consents` OR `the person to whom responsibility for the treatment of the accused is assigned by the court consents`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "without the consent of"
    ELSE JUST TRUE

-- 672.62(2): the court may direct that treatment of an accused be carried out pursuant to a disposition made under section 672.58 without the consent of the accused or a person who, according to the laws of the province where the disposition is made, is authorized to consent for the accused.
-- src:13789 | (2) The court may direct that treatment of an accused be carried out pursuant to a disposition made under section 672.58 without the consent of the accused or a person who, according to the laws of the province where the disposition is made, is authorized to consent for the accused.
@ref s 672.62(2) (src:13789)
GIVEN `it is a disposition made under section 672.58` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 672.62(2) the court may direct that treatment be carried out without the consent of the accused` MEANS
    IF `it is a disposition made under section 672.58`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "pursuant to a disposition made under section 672.58"

§ `Section 672.63 -- Effective date of disposition`

-- 672.63: a disposition shall come into force on the day on which it is made or on any later day that the court or Review Board specifies in it, and shall remain in force until the Review Board holds a hearing to review the disposition and makes another disposition.
-- The function answers whether the disposition is in force on a given day. Outside the period the text fixes in its own words the answer is JUST FALSE (the periods ruling of 2026-11-05).
-- src:13791 | 672.63 A disposition shall come into force on the day on which it is made or on any later day that the court or Review Board specifies in it, and shall remain in force until the Review Board holds a hearing to review the disposition and makes another disposition.
@ref s 672.63 (src:13791)
GIVEN `the day the disposition is made` IS A DATE
      `the later day that the court or Review Board specifies in the disposition` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the day the Review Board holds a hearing to review the disposition and makes another disposition` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the day asked about` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 672.63 the disposition is in force on the day` MEANS
    IF `the day asked about` AT LEAST `the day it comes into force` AND `it has not yet been replaced on the day asked about`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall come into force on the day on which it is made or on any later day that the court or Review Board specifies in it, and shall remain in force until the Review Board holds a hearing to review the disposition and makes another disposition"
    WHERE
        `the day it comes into force` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the later day that the court or Review Board specifies in the disposition`
            WHEN JUST later THEN later
            WHEN NOTHING THEN `the day the disposition is made`
        `it has not yet been replaced on the day asked about` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the day the Review Board holds a hearing to review the disposition and makes another disposition`
            WHEN JUST reviewed THEN `the day asked about` LESS THAN reviewed
            WHEN NOTHING THEN TRUE
